---
source: crates/zaun/src/cli.rs
expression: cmd.render_help().to_string()
---
Run Windows games through umu-run inside a per-game bubblewrap sandbox

Usage: zaun [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  open      Open Windows programs: start known ones, set up unknown ones
  launch    Launch a game
  stop      Stop a running game
  status    Show running games and the latest sessions
  list      List games
  add       Add a program to the library
  edit      Change a game's settings
  remove    Remove a game from the library
  show      Show a game's settings
  sandbox   Inspect sandboxes
  export    Export a game's settings as TOML
  import    Import a game's settings
  doctor    Check this system for everything Zaun needs
  runtimes  Manage compatibility layers
  steam     Games installed with Steam (shown when "Show my Steam games" is on)
  overlay   Show or hide the in-game overlay in the running Zaun (bind it to a key in your compositor, e.g. Shift+F1)
  update    Check for a newer version of Zaun, or install it (asks github.com; only while "Check for updates" is on)
  service   Keep Zaun running in the background so opened programs start at once
  help      Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -v, --verbose...  Increase log verbosity (-v debug, -vv trace)
      --add         Start (or focus) Zaun and open the add-game dialog
  -h, --help        Print help
  -V, --version     Print version
